1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,132
An oyster is a little jar of the sea

2
00:00:03,036 --> 00:00:05,756
it grew in. Every one on this platter tastes

3
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:06,812
of different water.

4
00:00:07,559 --> 00:00:10,417
For centuries, oysters were food for the poor. In

5
00:00:10,299 --> 00:00:12,879
New York, six cents bought all you could eat.

6
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:16,151
Then sewage closed the beds. The last one in

7
00:00:15,998 --> 00:00:19,437
New York shut in nineteen twenty-seven. Now a single

8
00:00:19,283 --> 00:00:21,446
oyster costs over three dollars.

9
00:00:22,227 --> 00:00:24,784
So why a dollar at five o'clock? The bar

10
00:00:24,676 --> 00:00:27,895
pays about seventy-seven cents for each one. After the

11
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:29,880
shucker is paid, it loses money.

12
00:00:30,538 --> 00:00:33,641
That's the trick. The cheap oyster fills the seats,

13
00:00:33,476 --> 00:00:35,115
and the drinks pay for it.

14
00:00:36,001 --> 00:00:39,347
The taste comes from survival. An oyster matches the

15
00:00:39,194 --> 00:00:41,878
salt around it by filling its cells with amino

16
00:00:41,771 --> 00:00:46,290
acids, mostly taurine. Saltier water, more savoury oyster.

17
00:00:47,466 --> 00:00:52,403
So place matters. Cold northern bays give briny oysters.

18
00:00:52,493 --> 00:00:56,420
The warm Gulf gives mild ones. The Pacific coast

19
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:58,533
tastes of cucumber and melon.

20
00:00:59,778 --> 00:01:03,914
Season matters too. Oysters are plumpest before they spawn

21
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:07,618
in summer. Then they turn milky, and warm water

22
00:01:07,464 --> 00:01:09,313
brings Vibrio bacteria.

23
00:01:10,245 --> 00:01:14,357
The priciest aren't a different animal, just older, rarer

24
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:17,724
or bigger. A Coffin Bay King grows six years

25
00:01:17,606 --> 00:01:19,988
and sold for a hundred Australian dollars.

26
00:01:20,851 --> 00:01:24,325
And a good one? Shut tight, heavy, full of

27
00:01:24,171 --> 00:01:27,088
liquor, smelling of the sea. Ask to see the

28
00:01:26,935 --> 00:01:27,808
tag.

